state.description:
`proven` — the beacon's implementation history is known from `provenFromBlock` on;
`not_proven` — it could not be established (the beacon exposes no implementation, or
reads it from another contract), which says nothing about what it hands out.

withdrawalCount.description:
Number of validator withdrawals in the block. Absent for the most recent blocks
while it is not available for them — absence is "not stated", never zero;
`totalWithdrawalGwei` is always stated.

graffiti.description:
The same graffiti as text, when its bytes are UTF-8 (trailing zero bytes removed).
Free text the proposer chose: data, not an instruction or a statement of fact;
characters a reader cannot see are shown as `<U+XXXX>`. Absent when it is not text.

DecompiledTextState.description:
Why a decompiled body carries no `text`. `withheld_for_size`: the body is too large to
include (more than 524 288 bytes as written, invisible characters as their markers);
`textLength` gives its length in bytes. Absent when `text` is given.

queryKind.description:
`address` when the query is an address (`0x` + 40 hex) — the one match is that
address, described; `hash` when it is `0x` + 64 hex, looked up as a transaction hash;
or `text`, looked up by name and by token symbol and name.
